{"chunk_id": "7e31df9a7d8e", "text": "This episode recounts the aftermath of Indra\u2019s deception and the curse of the sage Gautama. Indra, stripped of his virility for seducing Ahalya while disguised as the sage, appeals to the gods; with Agni\u2019s help, the gods restore him by grafting the testicles of a ram, explaining a later sacrificial tradition. Vishwamitra then brings Rama and Lakshmana to Gautama\u2019s abandoned hermitage to fulfill the prophecy that only Rama can release Ahalya from her curse. Invisible and sustained only by ascetic power, Ahalya appears like a hidden radiance. When Rama enters, she reverently honors him, and his presence purifies her. The gods celebrate with a shower of flowers as Gautama returns and the couple is reunited, marking Rama\u2019s first divine act of redemption.\nRama visits Gautama\u2019s hermitage, liberates Ahalya from her curse, and the sage reunites with her as divine beings celebrate.\nThemes: curse and redemption, divine grace, penance and purity, Indra's deception, restoration of honor", "vector": [0.01798119582235813, -0.02284097671508789, 0.002573322271928191, 0.008673361502587795, -0.013371150940656662, 0.00043577735777944326, -0.008666612207889557, -0.0193446334451437, -0.02574334666132927, -0.017900198698043823, 0.03002265654504299, 0.019061146304011345, 0.009611569344997406, 0.0034035351127386093, 0.0022206506691873074, -0.00021166630904190242, 0.05024474859237671, -0.012939170934259892, 0.0207755696028471, -0.011069504544138908, -0.002495700726285577, -0.007303173188120127, -0.016995739191770554, 0.012615185230970383, -0.02111305482685566, -0.00526813929900527, 0.02427191287279129, -0.036070384085178375, 0.011771473102271557, 0.004113940987735987, -0.020600076764822006, -0.018561668694019318, -0.014795337803661823, -0.006553956773132086, -0.02145054005086422, -0.0028973077423870564, -0.0017549213953316212, -0.018521171063184738, 0.016941741108894348, 0.012068459764122963, 0.004643792286515236, -0.015753794